---
import { LINKS } from "@/constants/links";
import { ROUTES } from "@/constants/routes";
import { SITE } from "@/constants/site";
import LegalLayout from "@/layouts/legal.astro";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description={`Terms for reading ${SITE.NAME} and for buying sponsorship placements.`}
  path={ROUTES.TERMS}
  updated="October 2026"
>
  <p>
    {SITE.NAME} is a free weekly newsletter about the shadcn/ui ecosystem, run
    by {SITE.AUTHOR.NAME} as an individual and published under {
      SITE.ORG.NAME
    }. By subscribing, reading the site, or buying a sponsorship you agree to
    these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>The newsletter</h2>
  <p>
    Subscribing is free. One issue goes out every Monday, and every issue is
    also published in the <a href={ROUTES.ISSUES} class="link">archive</a>. You
    can unsubscribe at any time from the link in every email. Linked projects
    belong to their authors; we don't endorse or guarantee third-party
    products.
  </p>

  <h2>Sponsorships</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href={ROUTES.SPONSOR} class="link">sponsor page</a> lists the
    placements we sell, their prices in USD, and the open issue weeks. When you
    buy a placement:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      You get your sponsor block (name, headline, description, link and image)
      in the issue(s) for the week(s) you picked, both in the email and on the
      issue's page on this site. A bundle covers four issues.
    </li>
    <li>
      Every booking is reviewed before it runs. We may ask you to change copy,
      and we decline content that is misleading, illegal, adult, gambling,
      crypto-investment, or unrelated to developers. A declined booking is
      refunded in full.
    </li>
    <li>
      You're responsible for your content and confirm you have the right to use
      the name, text, images and links you submit.
    </li>
    <li>
      We don't guarantee a number of opens, clicks or conversions.
    </li>
    <li>
      Weeks can be booked at least 3 days ahead. To move a week, email us
      before that issue goes out.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Cancellations and refunds are covered by the <a
      href={ROUTES.REFUNDS}
      class="link">refund policy</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2>Payments</h2>
  <p>
    Payments are processed by <a
      href="https://dodopayments.com"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
      class="link">Dodo Payments</a
    >, which acts as the merchant of record: Dodo Payments is the seller of
    record for your purchase and handles payment processing, sales tax and VAT,
    and receipts. Your purchase is also subject to Dodo Payments' buyer terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms; the date below shows the latest version, and
    bookings already paid keep the terms in place when you bought them.
    Questions? Email <a href={`mailto:${LINKS.EMAIL}`} class="link"
      >{LINKS.EMAIL}</a
    > or use the <a href={ROUTES.CONTACT} class="link">contact form</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
